From 1bc5cfd4a4430c63c5785d2b0c415e552a019809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:31:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] iio: qcom-smgr: fix the Z axis of the mount matrix

SMGR reports three-axis sensors in north-east-down coordinates. The
mount matrix swapped and negated X and Y but left Z alone, which makes
it a reflection (determinant -1) rather than a rotation, so it cannot
describe how a real part is mounted.

The result is visible on an LG V30 (US998) lying screen up on a desk:
in_accel_z_raw reads -9.71 m/s^2 and iio-sensor-proxy reports the tilt
as face-down. Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/mount-matrix.txt
expects +9.81 m/s^2 out of the screen in that position.

Negate Z as well. X and Y are unchanged, and iio-sensor-proxy only uses
the square of Z when working out screen rotation, so rotation is not
affected. The matrix is shared with the gyroscope and magnetometer,
which need the same right-handed frame.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index 3d622e80b..38b6ff5d7 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -374,7 +374,7 @@ static const struct iio_mount_matrix qcom_smgr_iio_mount_matrix = {
 	.rotation = {
 		"0", "-1", "0",
 		"-1", "0", "0",
-		"0", "0", "1"
+		"0", "0", "-1"
 	}
 };
 
